{{!
	Opening tag of the pinned placement of a pinnable region.

	Data from NotionComponentPinnableContainer::getTemplateData(), two keys and no others:
	string id container id stem, e.g. `notion-toc`. The rendered id appends `-pinned-container`,
		the same suffix NotionComponentPinnableHeader derives for data-pinned-container-id and
		pinnableElement.js resolves with document.getElementById, so it is never altered. Six
		stems reach the container family, so never branch on a particular id.
	bool is-pinned deliberately not read. Both containers are always emitted, because the script
		relocates the region between them without a reload and so needs both move targets in the
		DOM; whichever placement is inactive is legitimately empty. Callers guard only the
		CONTENT with this flag, never the container, which is what keeps the pinned region
		correct and fully styled when JavaScript is unavailable.

	Must be used with PinnableContainer/Close.mustache to avoid unclosed HTML tags. That closer
	is shared with the Unpinned variant, hence its position one directory up.
}}
<div id="{{id}}-pinned-container" class="notion-pinned-container">
